# TheKeyMachine changelog
#
# Format:
# version:
#   - kind: short description
#
# Supported kinds: new, changed, polish, bugfix.
# Rule: keep each version to 6 changes at most.
# Rule: sort entries by main group in this order: polish, bugfix, new, changed.
# Rule: keep descriptions short and efficient.
# Rule: mention each tool only once per version.
# Rule: focus on animation tool changes, visible workflow changes, and bugfixes.
# Rule: do not include repo housekeeping, docs, funding, metadata, or asset-only changes.
# Rule: avoid code technicalities such as modules, APIs, registries, packages, internal managers, or implementation refactors.
# Rule: rephrase technical changes into animator-facing behavior when there is a visible effect.
# Rule: keep entries broad and concise; include specifics only when needed to explain a bug.

0.1.45:
  - polish: Long tool operations keep progress and time remaining responsive while work continues
  - bugfix: Attribute Switcher can cancel multi-frame applies with Esc and no longer stalls in Normal or Super mode
  - bugfix: Copy and Paste Animation and Pose stay responsive during heavy copy operations
  - bugfix: Nudge keeps highlighted timeline ranges moving together with nudged keys
  - bugfix: Nudge snaps keys cleanly when a moved key lands on another key

0.1.44:
  - polish: Toolbars open and reload faster
  - bugfix: Reloading and unloading cleans up callbacks and leftover UI elements

0.1.43:
  - new: Temporal Controls builds a driven curve control for each selected object, with System, Position/Orientation space, and color, then Bake or Revert
  - changed: Locators removed
  - changed: Manipulators, Micro Move, Tracer, Temp Pivot, Follow Cam, and Animation Layers trimmed from the Graph Editor toolbar

0.1.42:
  - new: Global Curve reshapes selected or visible Graph Editor curves together with live time and tangent controls

0.1.41:
  - bugfix: Tooltips stay accurate and correctly localized across animation, selection, attribute, tangent, and tracer tools
  - new: Create and manage multiple tracers
  - new: Rotation-aware tracer offsets
  - changed: Auto Update is enabled by default with selectable performance presets

0.1.40:
  - bugfix: Toolbar alignment, pinning, and reloads stay responsive without clipped rows or menu errors

0.1.39:
  - bugfix: Copy and Paste Animation reliably recognizes the same control across full and short scene paths
  - bugfix: Smart Key and other layer-aware tools read animation layers without errors
  - changed: The codebase was restructured for clearer tool ownership and easier future development

0.1.38:
  - polish: Search and Hotkeys open faster and keep menu options clear and in sync
  - bugfix: Attribute Switcher stays responsive on large multi-control changes
  - bugfix: Mirror and opposite pasting work reliably across full rigs, animation ranges, and parented controls
  - bugfix: Snapshot Rig safely handles posed rigs and detects mirror behavior more reliably
  - bugfix: Sliders now create keys on frames without existing keys
  - changed: Cycle Matcher can match tangents only or include key values

0.1.37:
  - polish: Tool progress shows smooth second-by-second time remaining without item counters
  - bugfix: Rig analysis resolves opposite controls across separate branches and safely skips malformed attributes
  - new: Snapshot Rig saves default poses, opposite controls, and automatically tested mirror directions per rig
  - changed: Default, Opposite, and Mirror right-click menus expose their matching Snapshot actions

0.1.36:
  - bugfix: Attribute Switcher's Cancel and Esc reliably stop an in-progress switch in Normal and Super mode, and its popup selector no longer occasionally errors while dragging
  - bugfix: Cancelling Animation Recovery, World Space, or Copy and Paste Pose and Animation mid-operation now reverts cleanly instead of leaving a partial result

0.1.35:
  - polish: Tool progress is steadier, more responsive, and less intrusive
  - bugfix: Selection Sets and toolbar popups close reliably after losing focus
  - bugfix: Smart Key and Snap Keys run faster while respecting Channel Box channels, highlighted ranges, and selected animation layers
  - bugfix: World Space frame pastes keep timeline feedback and cleanup reliable
  - new: Anim Layer Weights displays live layer-weight curves on the timeline
  - changed: Anim Curve Tools share consistent targeting, concise feedback, and a tangent-aware key clipboard with channel remapping and relative pasting

0.1.34:
  - bugfix: Tooltips, shortcuts, and right-click action menus (including Bake, Share Keys, and Remove Redundant Keys) stay translated after switching languages
  - bugfix: Windows like About, Donate, Hotkeys, and Workspaces refresh immediately when you switch languages instead of needing a restart
  - new: Added Catalan, Chinese, Japanese, Korean, and Arabic translations across every menu, dialog, and hotkey editor

0.1.33:
  - polish: Fixing startup time by optimizing processes and deduping logic
  - bugfix: Workspaces update correctly on toolbar right click menu
  - new: Super mode to switch Rotation Orders almost instantly
  - new: Early stages of implementing different language translations

0.1.32:
  - polish: Tool actions share consistent progress feedback with automatic time estimates
  - bugfix: Simplify and Bake sliders preserve the intended animation curve tendency
  - new: Animation Recovery keeps resilient incremental checkpoints and alerts when an older scene file is opened
  - new: Attribute Switcher can apply different options across multiple controls
  - new: Anim Curve Tools adds refireable key and frame navigation with reliable channel-aware key pasting
  - changed: Copy Animation, Align, World Space and Relationship tools preserve the active animation-layer context

0.1.31:
  - polish: Attribute Switcher scrolls attributes lists within to be able to see them all!
  - bugfix: Smart Key handles exact subframes and mixed keyed or unkeyed selections
  - bugfix: Snap Keys merges multiple subframes per frame from object or range selections
  - bugfix: Fixed World Space toolbuttons, it bakes selected or visible ranges without removing outside keys
  - bugfix: Auto Hide Static Curves refreshes already-open Graph Editors reliably
  - changed: Align Objects uses the objecy keys and selects the target object at the end

0.1.30:
  - new: Toolbar workspaces (Standard, Professional, Minimal) switch pinned tools from the right-click menu

0.1.29:
  - polish: Reordered files to standarize all tools under tools/
  - bugfix: Copy Relationship pastes selected or playback ranges only on existing relationship-object keys
  - bugfix: Copy and Paste Pose and Animation handle remapped targets and single-object pastes reliably
  - bugfix: Smart Key supports subframes
  - bugfix: Snap Keys merges near-integer keys correctly
  - bugfix: Each Animation Offset gesture undoes in one step

0.1.28:
  - changed: Micro Move and Depth Mover now ship together across supported Maya versions and platforms with Shift/Control precision; Micro Move also keeps full-color cursors and reliable middle-button object drags

0.1.27:
  - new: Depth Mover pushes selected controls through camera depth with drag-adjusted sensitivity
  - new: Micro Move uses translate and rotate manipulators with Maya tool switching, cursor acceleration and modifiers

0.1.26:
  - new: Search finds and runs any TheKeyMachine tool

0.1.25:
  - changed: Animation curve tools now consistently respect selected Graph Editor keys, Channel Box channels and highlighted timeline ranges
  - changed: Smart Euler Filter unwraps only the active rotation keys while preserving the exact key selection
  - changed: Wave alternates positive and negative offsets per key with range-aware amplitude
  - changed: Tangent, alignment and snapping tools use the active animation context more consistently
  - polish: Blend to Buffer follows each curve's own buffered shape and rotates manual tangents only when necessary
  - bugfix: Static and redundant key cleanup stays scoped, and pin menus retain tool icons, hotkeys and shelf actions

0.1.24:
  - new: Custom Tools supports folders, local icons, toolbar pinning and button-triggered refresh
  - new: Auto Hide Static Animation Curves keeps the Graph Editor focused on animated channels
  - changed: Attribute Switcher and Orbit popups open beside their trigger on the correct screen
  - changed: Animation Offset and frame-based slider handles snap and tint accurately as the timeline changes
  - polish: Toolbar sections, Graph Editor placement, menus and in-view feedback are clearer and more consistent
  - bugfix: About and Follow Cam work reliably, and disabled online or Bug Report features stay hidden

0.1.23:
  - new: Frame-based sliders can pick and display independent timeline targets
  - changed: Buffer and Undo sliders blend animation curve shapes without moving keys
  - changed: Tangent sliders use contextual targets, mirrored blending and exact modes at full strength
  - changed: Time Offset preserves key timing while Stagger moves complete object animation
  - polish: Gap Stitcher, Noise, Wave, Infinity and World Space sliders produce more natural results
  - bugfix: Slider previews, generated keys, timeline picking and Undo now finish reliably

0.1.22:
  - changed: TKM menu commands now live in the main TKM Menu section
  - changed: Global Tools now appears before Background Runners in the toolbar
  - polish: Toolbar maintenance actions carry clearer toolbox tooltips
  - polish: Hotkeys window shows the same tooltip text as the matching tools
  - bugfix: TKM menu entries are available in the hotkeys list again
  - bugfix: Version metadata is synced across the package and installer

0.1.21:
  - new: Welcome prompt can add the TheKeyMachine shelf button after install
  - changed: Toolbar command routing is cleaner and more reliable
  - polish: Tooltips show assigned hotkeys and cleaner header actions
  - polish: Smart Manipulators now sit after Tangents in the toolbar
  - bugfix: Hotkeys window uses the correct command tooltip details
  - bugfix: Paste Animation is faster on dense animation clips

0.1.20:
  - polish: Some more tools have refined icons
